  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "LkW8IVQqDOmN4wgxmAW8weEhuJg=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:32:09.367Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The mechanism is an OpenCloud webhook dispatching a typed operation on document state change \u2014 the same document-state seam used for Alfresco and Nextcloud, applied to a newer platform.\n\nThe recorded reasoning is about timing rather than mechanism: it is proposed as a joint reference with Heinlein while the platform is still young. That is a stated rationale for approaching this lead now rather than a claim about the platform's capabilities, and it should be carried as such.\n\nThe single lead is Heinlein Support GmbH in Berlin, marked \"3 \u00b7 later\" \u2014 so the timing argument and the priority pull in opposite directions, which is worth resolving explicitly before the lead is worked. This is the second single-lead demo in this slice framed as a joint reference credited to the partner, the other being Caluma with Adfinis.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (1)\n\n**3 \u00b7 later**\n- Heinlein Support GmbH (DE Berlin) \u2014 https://heinlein-support.de\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> OpenCloud webhook dispatching a typed operation on document state change, proposed as a joint reference with Heinlein while the platform is still young.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:32:09.367824Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:32:09.367829Z"
    }
  },
